<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35381" root="قرأ" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَارِئٌ</span></b>  as an epithet applied to a she-camel; pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوَارِئُ</span>: see 1, former half. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>Reading,</i> or
<i>reciting,</i> the Kur-án [&amp;c.]; or <i>a reader,</i> or
<i>reciter,</i> thereof: (K, TA:) and sometimes the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>
is suppressed, so that one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَارٍ</span>: (TA:) pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرَأَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُرَّآءٌ</span> (S, O, Msb, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَارِئُونَ</span>. (Msb,
K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>syn. with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُرَّآءٌ</span>, q. v. (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  See
also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْءٌ</span>, first quarter, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا وَقْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَارِئِ الرِّيحِ</span> means <i>This is the time of the blowing
of the wind.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A5-  It is also said to signify
The <i>top,</i> or <i>upper part,</i> of a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصْر</span> [or pavilion,
&amp;c.]. (O.)

